ect analysis.", "newValue": "King's College London, established in 1829, is one of the oldest and most prestigious universities in the United Kingdom, located in the heart of London. Founded by King George IV and the Duke of Wellington, the institution has played a pivotal role in the development of higher education in Britain and beyond, contributing significantly to various fields including medicine, law, and the humanities. Its location in a cosmopolitan city has enabled it to attract a diverse body of students and faculty, enhancing its global influence and academic rigor.

